concept schema {
  name     = "Schema & Decorators"
  summary  = "Decorators that describe a document's legal structure, validated by wcl check."
  related  = [block_schema, document_schema, ref_integrity, child_count_constraints, records, fields_blocks, connections]
  audience = :both
  body {
    p "Decorators (written `@name` or `@name(args)`) attach schema metadata to declarations and fields. Together they describe a document's legal structure, which `wcl check` validates."
    p "- [Block Schema](concept_block_schema) — `@block`, `@inline`, `@child`/`@children`, `@default`."
    p "- [Document Schema](concept_document_schema) — `@document` roots and per-namespace merging."
    p "- [Referential Integrity](concept_ref_integrity) — validating id references with `@ref`."
    p "- [Child-count Constraints](concept_child_count_constraints) — `max_children` and `required_children`."
    p "The full decorator tables — declaration and field decorators — live in the [Schema decorators](fact_field_decorators) fact. Numeric and string/list constraints (`@min`, `@max`, `@non_empty`) are covered alongside type aliases under [type constraints](fact_type_constraints)."
  }
}
